Intercom development ledger

Status: ACTIVE
Milestone: Continuous public-safe development history
Dependencies: None

Purpose:
  Preserve actions, effects, rationale, mechanisms, evidence, and next consequences.
  This perpetual ledger is excluded from workstream-to-issue mapping.

Tasks:
  Append significant development entries without rewriting prior evidence.

Acceptance criteria:
  Entries distinguish plans, implementation, technical evidence, human acceptance,
  and publication. Private continuity, credentials, and raw chats stay excluded.

Completion evidence:
  This ledger is ongoing, not a finite feature deliverable.

Completion log:
  2026-11-10 - Project foundation authored.
    Action: inspected the clean repository and adopted the development manual.
    Effect: project entry points, contributor rules, product brief, and numbered
      workstreams now exist.
    Why: the original README states direction but not implementation decisions.
    Mechanism: separate product facts, workstream contracts, public history,
      remote tracking policy, and ignored private context.
    Evidence: initial README-only tree at 68385a3; no issues or linked Project.
    Limit: no app, selected stack, executable, build/test suite, or deployment.
    Next: verify remote tracking and context registration before closing ic-01.
  2026-11-10 - Foundation and tracking completed locally.
    Action: registered owned context, created private Intercom Project 13,
      mirrored both workstreams as issues, and added issue-backed Project items.
    Effect: ic-01 is complete; ic-02 remains unstarted.
    Why: resumability and explicit product decisions prevent speculative setup
      from being mistaken for an implemented assistant.
    Mechanism: stable workstream IDs, local backlinks, actual discovered status
      options, manual conflict-aware reconciliation, and checked mesh publication.
    Evidence: four eight-field TODOs, two backlinks, seven local links; Git ignores
      private context; mesh build discovers 40 contexts including Intercom;
      remote #1 CLOSED/COMPLETED/Done and #2 OPEN/Todo independently read back.
    Limit: no automatic sync runtime, application build, user acceptance,
      commit, push, release, or deployment.
    Next: define the product workflow and first vertical slice under ic-02.
  2026-11-10 - Voice/mesh architecture and qualification roadmap recorded.
    Action: captured spoken assistant requirements and explicit scope choices;
      inspected CareerOS graph source, installed Agency/Copilot help, mesh schema,
      public SDK docs and local/cloud speech references.
    Effect: ic-02 is IN_PROGRESS; ic-04 through ic-07 are gated future work.
    Why: existing Agency sessions and trustworthy completion matter more than
      a visually convincing shell around an unverified connector.
    Mechanism: separate wake/dialogue, session routing, connector, durable jobs,
      evidence-backed graph activity and completion speech; compare speech before
      choosing a provider. Keep context topology distinct from live telemetry.
    Evidence: docs/product-brief.md, docs/architecture.md, docs/speech-options.md
      and docs/roadmap.md distinguish user choices, proposals and unproven behavior.
    Limit: user chose documentation only. No app, selected stack/provider, audio
      capture, model download, session dispatch, live attachment or quality claim.
    Next: reconcile tracking and continuity; wait for separately authorized
      Agency/speech qualification before implementation.
  2026-11-10 - Voice-roadmap tracking reconciled.
    Action: checked previous normalized body hashes/states before updating #2
      and creating #3 through #6 from public-safe workstream projections.
    Effect: all six workstreams have actual issue-backed Project items/backlinks.
    Evidence: independent full remote read verifies bodies, states/status IDs,
      six issues/items, private Project visibility and sole repository link;
      original #1 is unchanged. docs/github-tracking.md records final mappings
      and read-back hashes. Eight TODO schemas and acyclic dependencies checked.
    Limit: manual reconciliation, not a sync service; no runtime qualification.
    Next: persist the design milestone and refresh owned Context Mesh continuity.
  2026-11-10 - Processing priority requirement clarified.
    Action: recorded performance/speed as the top priority and default, with
      selectable priorities; accuracy remains important.
    Effect: design, speech comparison and future qualification/slice criteria
      now include profiles, useful-response latency and resource/error budgets.
    Mechanism: propose Speed/performance, Balanced and Accuracy modes, persist
      the selected mode and apply changes only at request boundaries. Exact
      labels, engine settings and numerical targets remain unqualified.
    Limit: no implementation or performance claim; permissions, correct targeting,
      cloud consent and truthful completion remain mandatory in every profile.
    Evidence: same #2/#4/#5/#6 bodies updated after all six saved baselines
      matched; final independent read verifies complete descriptions, unchanged
      issue-backed items/stages and all backlinks. No duplicate tracking created.
